2026-06-09 13:47:40.672 [info] [Terminal] Executing command {"terminalId":1,"command":"python -c \"\nimport time\nimport random\n\nfrom src.optimization.routing import find_optimal_route\n\n# Simulate what the scheduler does - many calls with 15 destinations\nrandom.seed(42)\nlocations = [f'LOC{i:03d}' for i in range(60)]\n\n# Create a travel matrix like in the test\ntm = {}\nrng = random.Random(42)\nfor loc1 in locations:\n    tm[loc1] = {}\n    for loc2 in locations:\n        if loc1 == loc2:\n            tm[loc1][loc2] = 0.0\n        elif loc2 in tm and loc1 in tm[loc2]:\n            tm[loc1][loc2] = tm[loc2][loc1]\n        else:\n            tm[loc1][loc2] = round(rng.uniform(0.1, 0.8), 2)\n\n# Time 80 calls with ~12 destinations each (like test 2)\nt0 = time.time()\nfor i in range(80):\n    start = f'LOC{(i*10) % 60:03d}'\n    dests = random.sample([l for l in locations if l != start], 12)\n    find_optimal_route(start, dests, tm)\nelapsed = time.time() - t0\nprint(f'80 calls with 12 destinations: {elapsed:.3f}s')\n\n# Time 250 calls with ~18 destinations (like test 3)\nt0 = time.time()\nfor i in range(250):\n    start = f'LOC{(i*10) % 60:03d}'\n    dests = random.sample([l for l in locations if l != start], 18)\n    find_optimal_route(start, dests, tm)\nelapsed = time.time() - t0\nprint(f'250 calls with 18 destinations: {elapsed:.3f}s')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":60000}
